Subject: [PATCH] SkyHand: Skip block updates players cannot see

Every block change is sent to each player who has the chunk loaded, and
the client rebuilds the 16x16x16 mesh around it. Two kinds of change
show nothing on screen:
- a property that no model, block entity packet or client logic reads:
  tripwire powered/disarmed (items falling through cactus farm string),
  hopper enabled, dispenser/dropper triggered, note block powered, leaves
  distance/persistent, beehive honey level below 5;
- a cactus grown where it cannot stay (cactus farms): it breaks on the
  next tick, and players still get that break (particles, sound, item).
A grown cactus still standing at the next broadcast is sent then.
Changes back to the same state on purpose (block entity data, plugins
resending a block) are always sent. Config key
performance.optimizations.hidden-block-updates.enabled.

